cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Pairwise70: Advanced Pooling Methods for Pairwise Meta-Analysis"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this
  file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mahmood
    family-names: Arai
    email: mahmood726@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/mahmood726-cyber/hta-evidence-integrity"
url: "https://github.com/mahmood726-cyber/hta-evidence-integrity"
abstract: >-
  An R package of six advanced pooling estimators developed against the
  Pairwise70 collection of pairwise meta-analysis datasets extracted from
  Cochrane systematic reviews. Provides MAFI-weighted pooling
  (stability + precision), adaptive robust pooling
  (heterogeneity-driven multi-estimator weighting), sequential influence
  trimming, a unified bias-stability framework that combines trim-and-fill
  with leave-one-out diagnostics, an ensemble that averages the above, and a
  side-by-side comparison helper. Intended for meta-research, methodological
  studies, and software validation in meta-analysis.
keywords:
  - meta-analysis
  - pooling
  - random-effects
  - publication-bias
  - stability
  - Cochrane
  - R
